From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:31:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: preserve MAC TX on bridge detach

Leaving an offloaded bridge clears the MAC TX gate while the physical
link stays up. On IPQ9574 this also drops packets directed to the port
by EDMA, breaking standalone and software-bridged traffic.

Disable switch forwarding through the port STP state while retiring
the membership. Restore the forwarding state after successful cleanup
and leave the physical TX gate under the phylink callbacks.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_bridge.c
@@ -896,8 +896,9 @@
 			ppe_bridge_vsi_quarantine(pb, vsi, err);
 }
 
-/* Tear down a leaving port or unwind a failed join. Gate the port and
- * stop learning before switchdev replays deletions that can retire a VSI.
+/* Block switch forwarding and learning before switchdev replays deletions
+ * that can retire a VSI. The MAC TX gate follows the physical link and
+ * also controls frames sent from the CPU directly to the port.
  */
 static void ppe_bridge_port_detach(struct ppe_bridge *pb,
 				   struct net_device *dev, bool offloaded)
@@ -908,8 +909,8 @@
 	bool vlan_aware = p->vsi < 0;
 	int err, ret, i;
 
+	err = ppe_port_stp_state_set(ppe_dev, port, PPE_STP_STATE_DISABLED);
 	ppe_bridge_port_offload_mark_set(dev, false);
-	err = ppe_port_bridge_txmac_set(ppe_dev, port, false);
 	ret = ppe_port_bridge_learning_set(ppe_dev, port, false);
 	if (!err)
 		err = ret;
@@ -1042,14 +1043,6 @@
 			goto err_detach;
 	}
 
-	/* The bridge TX MAC gates packets forwarded to the port by the
-	 * hardware bridge, it is kept disabled while a port is not
-	 * offloaded.
-	 */
-	ret = ppe_port_bridge_txmac_set(ppe_dev, port, true);
-	if (ret)
-		goto err_detach;
-
 	if (vsi >= 0)
 		ppe_bridge_fdb_member_set(pb, vsi, port, true);
 	ppe_bridge_port_offload_mark_set(dev, true);
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_config.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_config.c
@@ -2205,28 +2205,6 @@
 }
 
 /**
- * ppe_port_bridge_txmac_set - Enable or disable the bridge TX MAC of a port
- * @ppe_dev: PPE device
- * @port: PPE port to configure
- * @enable: Enable or disable the bridge TX MAC
- *
- * The bridge TX MAC gates the egress of packets forwarded to the port by
- * the L2 bridge, it does not affect packets transmitted by the CPU with
- * an explicit destination port.
- *
- * Return: 0 on success, negative error code on failure.
- */
-int ppe_port_bridge_txmac_set(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev, int port,
-			      bool enable)
-{
-	u32 reg = PPE_PORT_BRIDGE_CTRL_ADDR + PPE_PORT_BRIDGE_CTRL_INC * port;
-
-	return regmap_update_bits(ppe_dev->regmap, reg,
-				  PPE_PORT_BRIDGE_TXMAC_EN,
-				  enable ? PPE_PORT_BRIDGE_TXMAC_EN : 0);
-}
-
-/**
  * ppe_port_bridge_learning_set - Control hardware FDB learning of a port
  * @ppe_dev: PPE device
  * @port: PPE port to configure
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_config.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_config.h
@@ -368,8 +368,6 @@
 			unsigned int port_bitmap, int svid, int cvid,
 			int vsi, bool add_svid, bool add_cvid);
 int ppe_eg_xlt_rule_clear(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev, int index);
-int ppe_port_bridge_txmac_set(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev, int port,
-			      bool enable);
 int ppe_port_bridge_learning_set(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev, int port,
 				 bool enable);
 int ppe_port_shaper_set(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev, int port, u64 rate,
--- a/Documentation/networking/qualcomm-ppe-offload.rst
+++ b/Documentation/networking/qualcomm-ppe-offload.rst
@@ -73,10 +73,12 @@
 L2 bridge offload
 -----------------
 
-A VLAN-unaware software bridge is backed by one VSI; joining binds the
-port to the VSI and enables its bridge TX MAC. Leaving retires the
-port membership and parks the last VSI before flushing and verifying
-its address table. A VSI with uncertain hardware state stays reserved.
+A VLAN-unaware software bridge is backed by one VSI. Joining binds
+the port to the VSI. Leaving blocks switch forwarding through the
+port's STP state, retires the port membership and parks the last VSI
+before flushing and verifying its address table. The link controls
+MAC TX so a detached port can immediately transmit for Linux again.
+A VSI with uncertain hardware state stays reserved.
 The CPU port is a member of every VSI: packets without an FDB hit
 flood to the CPU and reach the software ports of the bridge (wireless
 interfaces). Received packets carry skb->offload_fwd_mark and all
